cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project Nurse Ratchet: a therapeutic agent loop with auditable psychological modelling"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
abstract: >-
  A dependency-ordered stack of four layers: a trait and affect model, a
  psychological network in which constructs are nodes and regularised partial
  correlations are edges, a compiled-inference layer that turns repeated graph
  evaluation into graded prototypes, and a realtime loop that triages risk before
  any stance is scored. Ships with the evaluation instruments that grade each
  layer, including a labelled corpus with development and holdout splits, and a
  publication gate that refuses to ship evidence about identifiable people.
  Named for Nurse Ratched, who administers care as control in a register
  reasonable enough to be mistaken for help. The name is the warning, not the
  aspiration.
authors:
  - name: "Project Nurse Ratchet contributors"
keywords:
  - digital mental health
  - just-in-time adaptive intervention
  - network psychometrics
  - recognition-primed decision making
  - graph neural network
  - evaluation
  - open science
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Network analysis of multivariate data in psychological science"
    authors:
      - family-names: Borsboom
      - family-names: Deserno
      - family-names: Rhemtulla
    journal: "Nature Reviews Methods Primers"
    year: 2021
    notes: "The node-and-edge framing this project's construct graph follows."
  - type: article
    title: "A recognition-primed decision (RPD) model of rapid decision making"
    authors:
      - family-names: Klein
    year: 1993
    notes: "Intuition as compiled inference, which is what intuition.py implements."
  - type: article
    title: "Just-in-Time Adaptive Interventions (JITAIs) in mobile health"
    authors:
      - family-names: Nahum-Shani
    journal: "Annals of Behavioral Medicine"
    year: 2018
    notes: "The sense-decide-deliver shape of rt_agent.py, including the timing requirement."
  - type: article
    title: "ELIZA - a computer program for the study of natural language communication between man and machine"
    authors:
      - family-names: Weizenbaum
    journal: "Communications of the ACM"
    year: 1966
    notes: "The cautionary effect whose machinery this project grades. The name
      itself is Nurse Ratched's, not ELIZA's -- see the abstract."
# repository-code, url and the author's identity are added at publication.
# They are deliberately absent rather than guessed: a citation file that points
# at a URL nobody has reserved is worse than one that says it will be added.
